## The disagreement

Two notes carried a CONTRADICTS edge over `ProcessorFilter` semantics:

- **d7ef28bc** - "The `"*"` wildcard in a ProcessorFilter is honored only in documentId": `"*"` is special-cased for `documentId` alone; in `documentType`, `scope` and `branch` it is compared as a literal string and therefore matches nothing real.
- **6a3275cd** - "Processors implement IProcessor with onOperations...": as originally written, generalized that ProcessorFilter arrays take `["*"]` to mean "all".

## Evidence (installed source, not documentation)

`@powerhousedao/reactor@6.2.2-dev.47`, `dist/index.js`, `matchesFilter(op, filter)`:

```js
if (filter.documentType && filter.documentType.length > 0) {
  if (!filter.documentType.includes(op.context.documentType)) return false;
}
if (filter.scope && filter.scope.length > 0) {
  if (!filter.scope.includes(op.context.scope)) return false;
}
if (filter.branch && filter.branch.length > 0) {
  if (!filter.branch.includes(op.context.branch)) return false;
}
if (filter.documentId && filter.documentId.length > 0) {
  if (!filter.documentId.includes("*") && !filter.documentId.includes(op.context.documentId)) return false;
}
return true;
```

Only the `documentId` branch tests for `"*"`. The other three do a plain `includes` against the operation's context value. d7ef28bc describes the shipped behaviour exactly.

Two further facts checked at 6.2.2-dev.47:

1. **6a3275cd was already corrected on 2026-08-13.** Its current body states the same per-field rule verbatim - "The `"*"` wildcard is honored **only in `documentId`**" - so the two notes no longer disagree. The CONTRADICTS edge points at a superseded revision.
2. **The codegen defect d7ef28bc flagged has since been fixed.** `@powerhousedao/codegen@6.2.2-dev.47` emits `documentId: ["*"]` together with `scope: ["global"]` (relational template) or with no `scope` key at all (analytics template), and both templates now carry the comment `Only \`documentId\` honours "*", so "*" elsewhere would match nothing.` No template emits `scope: ["*"]` any more.

## Disposition

Dissolved. There is no live disagreement: both notes assert the rule the source implements. What remained wrong was d7ef28bc's own framing - it still described the sibling note as mistaken and the codegen template as broken, both true at v6.2.2-dev.45 and false at v6.2.2-dev.47. A dated correction paragraph was appended to that note on 2026-08-16. The CONTRADICTS edge is retained as provenance of the correction rather than deleted.
